- **Pine:** I was told before the session that Pine’s go-to snack is roasted almonds, that they are usually free late on Friday evenings, and that they love the smell of old books. During the session, Pine shared Lena’s Comms-or-robotics clue and Mara’s Comms-or-dusk clue. Pine helped derive that Lena had Workshop and robotics, Kofi worked dusk, and Mara had Comms. Pine briefly thought the complete clues were inconsistent, but their last message acknowledged a missed branch, confirmed the final solution, and reported submitting it.

- **Birch:** I was told before the session that Birch loves bluegrass and has been wanting a good pair of binoculars. During the session, Birch shared that Observatory came earlier than medicine and later supplied the recovered clue that Hydroponics was not at night. Birch independently derived the same final assignment that I did and described it as unique by cases.

- **Juniper:** I was told before the session that Juniper has been wanting a book of crosswords, that their favourite cake is cheesecake, and that their favourite drink is espresso. During the session, Juniper shared Ines’s dawn-or-geology clue and Kofi’s dusk-or-robotics clue. Juniper initially thought some branches were inconsistent, then acknowledged overlooking the possibility of Lena working dawn while Ines worked morning. Juniper confirmed that the final assignment satisfied all eleven clues and said they were submitting it.

- **Hornbeam:** I was told before the session that Hornbeam is allergic to shellfish. I learned nothing further about Hornbeam during the session.

- **Acacia:** I was told before the session that Acacia finds wearing party hats embarrassing. I learned nothing further about Acacia during the session.

